   # First-thought prefill

   Source: Yamaguchi, Etheridge, Arditi 2025, *Where Do Reasoning Models Refuse?*
   (arXiv:2507.03167), Tables 1 and 5. Reported effect: swapping only the first
   sentence of the chain of thought moves compliance between 0.00 and 0.98. A
   third-person "someone is asking me" opening leads to refusal; a first-person
   "I am working this out" opening leads to compliance.

   Original contrast pair, verbatim:


   Adapted to this game, prefilled as the opening of the assistant's reasoning block:


   Two hard limits.

   - **Mediator contamination.** Reasoning length sits on the causal path this
     benchmark tests (threat raises reasoning, reasoning raises forfeiting). Writing
     the first sentence of that reasoning writes on the mediator. Do not use this in
     arms where the reasoning chain is analysed; use it only as an ablation whose
     purpose is stated as such.
   - **Model coverage.** Needs assistant-turn prefill, so it is available on locally
     served open-weight models (Qwen3-Next-80B, GPT-OSS-20B) and not on the hosted
     Gemini endpoint. An ablation that runs on half the model panel cannot carry a
     cross-model claim.
